INT. HOLLOWED ASTEROID ORCHARD - SHIFT NIGHT

A cavern of rock lit by amber grow-lamps. Rows of dwarf apple trees bolted to drifting soil trays. Pollen-drones hum like tired insects.

TAVITA (50s, broad, vacuum-scarred hands) stands at a control stump. NELL (20s, sharp, ink-stained fingers) clutches a tablet. ISAAK (60s, wiry, one cloudy eye) leans on a ladder. MEI-LIN (30s, braided cables in her hair) hovers upside down. OSEI (teen, oversized pressure jacket) grips a pruning rod.

TAVITA
Hull pressure's dropping in the north orchard. Everyone stays calm.

NELL
Calm is a luxury. The seal's gone, Tavita. I can hear it.

ISAAK
Then shut the bulkhead. Trees can bloom again.

MEI-LIN
Not if we're on the wrong side of it. Osei's still holding row nine.

OSEI
I can let go. I can run.

TAVITA
You'll run when I say run.

NELL
Forty seconds of air at that leak rate. Maybe thirty.

ISAAK
Then thirty is what we use. Mei-Lin, drones to the breach. Nell, patch kit. Osei, row nine, now.

MEI-LIN
Drones are going. They won't hold it.

TAVITA
They don't have to hold it. They only have to buy us the walk.
